    "question": {
      ":question/id": "73adea87-cad2-5e92-8eac-3f48d0a8cdd2",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-28-topic-audit-3/published-probe/17592186096814/4c083038a5e885387eb7b2f3d996e2a6d137d73fdb5db2be4e76a146ca33b198-prompt.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-28-topic-audit-3/published-probe/17592186096814/4c083038a5e885387eb7b2f3d996e2a6d137d73fdb5db2be4e76a146ca33b198-solution.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4)^2+(2)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+4} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $2 \\sqrt{5}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{10}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
